"/blog/8": "<p> We operate across Poland — Lower Silesia, Opole, Greater Poland and Lubusz voivodeships</p> <section><a href=\"/blog\"><p> Back to blog</p></a>🛋️ Cleaning <h1>How to Count Sofa Seats?</h1> 2025-03-02 2 min <p>One seat is approximately 50–60 cm wide. The number of cushions hints at the number of seats, and armrests reduce usable space.</p><p>To count seats correctly, measure the total sofa length and divide by 55 cm. Consider body size — larger people need more space. Armrests take up room, so actual seating may be less than expected. This matters when ordering upholstery cleaning — pricing often depends on the number of seats.</p> <h2> Comments (0)</h2> <p>No comments yet. Be the first!</p> </section>",
"/blog/9": "<p> We operate across Poland — Lower Silesia, Opole, Greater Poland and Lubusz voivodeships</p> <section><a href=\"/blog\"><p> Back to blog</p></a>🌬️ Drying <h1>Why Dry Furniture After Cleaning?</h1> 2025-03-06 3 min <p>After cleaning, residual moisture can lead to mold and bad odors. Professional drying is an essential step for quality upholstery care.</p><p>Many people think air-drying is enough after cleaning. But without forced drying, moisture penetrates deep into the padding, creating a perfect environment for bacteria and mold.</p><p>🌬️ Why is drying so important?</p><p>💧 Residual moisture is furniture's enemy. After extraction, 10–15% moisture remains. Without drying it can linger 24–48 hours, causing:</p><p>• Mold and mildew inside the padding • Musty, unpleasant odors • Foam and stuffing deformation • Water stains on fabric</p><p>⏱️ What does professional drying provide?</p><p>✔️ Reduces drying time from 24–48 hours to 2–4 hours ✔️ 100% mold prevention ✔️ Preserves padding shape and structure ✔️ Eliminates water marks and stains ✔️ Furniture is ready to use within hours</p><p>🎉 Promotion: furniture drying — FREE!</p><p>We use powerful professional turbo dryers that evenly dry upholstery and padding. This is especially important for mattresses — sleeping on a damp mattress is not only unpleasant but also a health risk.</p> <h2> Comments (0)</h2> <p>No comments yet. Be the first!</p> </section>",
